+# Testing Your Next Chapter
+
+## Core idea
+
+Career change becomes clearer through small, deliberate experiments—not more private reflection. The lesson moves from a closed “thought loop” into an evidence-rich field test, then resolves into three practical experiments.
+
+## Visual direction
+
+An editorial field notebook meets a clean research dashboard. A gold route line travels across navy and paper surfaces, collecting evidence cards as it goes. The three experiments become distinct, numbered stations: conversation, trial project, and shadow day.
+
+## Story arc
+
+1. Contrast the familiar reflect-first advice with Ibarra’s act-first finding.
+2. Show why imagination remains constrained by past experience.
+3. Turn action into visible evidence: feedback, texture, energy, people, and correction.
+4. Introduce three low-risk experiments.
+5. Narrow each experiment to one answerable question.
+6. End on the value of evidence—even when it changes the direction.
+
